    code -1" instead of retrying, diverging from the C++'s `waitNoHang` loop
    (verified against the installed std source: `Child::try_wait` uses plain
    `cvt`, not `cvt_r`, so EINTR is not retried internally) — would have
    falsely reported exit, dropped live stdout/stderr pipes early, and leaked
    a zombie. Fixed: loop and retry on `ErrorKind::Interrupted`, matching
    `waitNoHang` exactly.
